  "$rooms": "weight: share of the floor a room wants; minSide: its narrowest width. A kitchen's `run` comes first: counter pieces side by side along one wall, one of each `with` slot (sink, stove, maybe a dishwasher) among plain `segments`, `length` tiles in all. Furniture is placed against the walls in this order (the pieces that must come first, then `dining`, then the rest): `one` picks one of the ids, `chance` (default 1) whether it comes at all, `count` how many, `opposite` puts it across the room from another (a TV facing the sofa). `dining`: a table standing free in the room with `seats` chairs (one kind, picked from `chairs`) round it, each facing it; with `wall`, against a wall with its chairs at its front (a desk). `surfaces`: small things put on tops of the kinds in `on` (counter, table, low, desk, shelf), the emptiest top first (`minSide`: only tops at least so wide, m). Then `wall`, `ceiling` and `rug` slots add things that take no floor space (content `layer`; only things nobody uses): pictures and curtains on walls (curtains over windows; `over`: on the wall behind one of those pieces if the room has one, like a mirror over the basin), lamps from the ceiling, a rug in the middle of the room. Rooms short of light get more ceiling lights (`lights` below).",
